<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
    Terrathyst: material used for building, stuffables, and some simple weapons
    Prismite: material used for higher tier weapons, armor, and buildings. Can be aquired by charing terrathyst
    Biothite: compressed prismite combined with sunsap. Used for high tier structures, armor, and weapons
    Metajade: jade charged with large amounts of shocksap or starsap. Used as a capacitor for weapons and structures that require high charge.
    Solarite: rare material only found in specific ways. Used to create highest-tier structures and weapons.
    Gravitite: special material found in specific ways. Used to create weapons, structures, and implants that manipulate gravity.-->

<Defs>
  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>ET_CrystalCrucible</defName>
    <label>prismite crucible</label>
    <description>A crystal chamber that snakes deep into the planet. This particular structure holds large amounts of shocksap, which is generally used for creating and evolving lithoid weapons and items.
This vessel can take a terrathyst core and use it as a catalyst to form a new, random lithic weapon. Adittionally, it can evolve most lithoid weapons as long as the desired weapon, and the required items, are near the crucible.
Lithic weapons are durable and unmoving. They take a longer time to evolve when compared to organic or hybrid weapons, and some weapons can take multiple quadrums to even acquire.</description>
